@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ The [generated tool reference](../../../docs/agents/mcp-tools.md) lists every to
 - `add_operation { "kind": string, "tool"?: string, "name"?: string, "source"?: string, "params"?: object }`: Add an operation to the active setup. `source` is `"stock"` (the default), a model name, or the name of a placed DXF profile (#1862: 2D milling, plasma and wire EDM kinds only; a kind that needs a solid model refuses a profile by name, and a 3D kind refuses a setup that has only a stock and a profile). `tool` is required for every kind where `list_operation_types` lists `"mounts_tool": true` (including `Wire Contour` with a `Wire` tool such as `"EDM-W025"`); only a kind with `"mounts_tool": false` omits `"tool"`.
 - **Wire Contour (#532, #1108, #2011)**: a 2-axis, constant-taper, or 4-axis wire EDM cut of one closed profile (a model's through silhouette or picked edges) or an open run (`side: "left"|"right"|"centre"` - left / right put the kerf beside their travel, centre cuts a slit along the run itself). Mount a wire EDM first: built-in `"Sodick ALC400G"` or `"AGIECUT Classic 2S (template)"` via `load_machine { "builtin": "..." }` (plus `edit_machine` to add `edm.conditions` and any `edm.codes`), or `load_machine { "path": "<.mch>" }` with an `edm.conditions` table. Add a `Wire` tool (`add_tool { "catalog": "EDM-W025", "holder": "none" }`, or a custom tool with `kind: "wire"`, `diameter` 0.02-1.0 mm, `rpm: 0`). Then `add_operation { "kind": "Wire Contour", "tool": "EDM-W025", "source": "<model>", "params": { "condition": "<condition id>", "side": "die"|"punch"|"left"|"right"|"centre", "picks": { "start": [[x, y]] } } }`. All fields (`list_operation_types { "kind": "wire_contour" }`): `top_z`, `bottom_z`, `condition`, `side`, `picks`, `start`, `tabs`, `capture`, `both_pieces_restrained`, `stock_centered_in_xy_travel`, `taper_deg`, `burnout_clearance`, `clearance`, `skims`, `four_axis`, `sharp_corners`, `overlap` (the closing overlap, mm, added to the seam lap; 0 is the plain lap), `lead_arc_radius`, `compensation`; `edit_operation` patches any of them. `compensation` (#4134, absent = `"computer"`, the wire-centre path) is `"control"` (the post writes the part contour under `G41`/`G42` with one register for each pass, the rough pass first, and `G40` on the lead-out; each register must hold that pass's kerf offset, wire radius + spark gap, which the program comment states) or `"wear"` (the wire-centre path under `G41`/`G42`; the register holds only the wear delta). Both need a closed die or punch profile with the straight lead and no taper, 4-axis cut, tabs, burnout or exit pick (refused at the command door), and a post that writes the offset (`"Sodick Wire EDM (LN2W)"`); other posts refuse the offset by name. Refusals arrive as tool errors in the command's words: missing or non-wire tool, no or unknown condition, a condition with no gap or wire diameter, or `taper_deg` past `edm.max_taper_deg`; the start hole and the corner minimum are refused at `generate`; a stated `overlap` beside a burnout, a 4-axis cut or a nonzero taper is refused by name, and an open run's `skims` rethread in the air between passes, each pass verified and posted at its own kerf. Post with `"Generic ISO Wire EDM"` (vertical, skims, constant taper, and 4-axis via `edm.codes`), `"Sodick Wire EDM (Mark 21)"` (vertical 2-axis only; refuses taper and 4-axis), or `"Agie Wire EDM (AgieVision)"` (an AgieVision job directory of ISO, SBR and SBL files for `"AGIECUT Classic 2S (template)"` with condition `AGIE_QN2`, one straight-sided vertical punch (`source: "<model>"`, `side: "punch"`) in 15, 20, 40 or 80 mm stock, or one convex die opening (`side: "die"`, the picked edge chains of the upper rim through `set_operation_geometry`) in a 20 mm plate, or one straight open cutoff (`side: "left"|"right"`, one picked X- or Y-parallel wall edge across the 20 mm stock, no `start`, `both_pieces_restrained` and `stock_centered_in_xy_travel` true, `clearance` at most 3.6, option `separationLengthMm: 0`), and 0.25 mm wire; punch reentrant corners are checked, not refused: each inside corner must be reached by the rough offset of the selected thickness within 0.002 mm, every segment must hold both corner joins, nonadjacent faces must keep the swept rough passes apart, and the entry must be on a straight exterior face; a notch that fails these checks is refused, see `docs/decisions/2956-agie-reentrant-punch.md` and `docs/user-guide/agie-wire-edm.md`); milling posts refuse wire cuts by name. Neither built-in wire `.mch` ships with `edm.conditions`, and the wire posts are not exercised on a physical EDM control. `lead_arc_radius` (mm, absent or `null` = the straight lead, #3991) states a tangent arc lead-in and lead-out on a selected DXF chain's vertical single pass: it must be more than the kerf offset of the resolved condition (wire radius + spark gap; refused at the command door, and again at `generate` for a loaded file), the start hole must stand more than twice the radius off the path, and a lead nearer the profile than the kerf offset is refused by name; beside an open run, tabs, skims, a taper, a burnout, a 4-axis cut or an exit pick it is refused at the command door.
 - **Sinker electrode (#547, #1156)**: `electrode_from_faces { "name": string, "picks": [face ids], "undersize"?: number, "condition"?: string, "setup"?: string, "orbit"?: number, "stub": number, "pickup": number }` generates a sinker EDM electrode from the picked faces of a cavity (its level floor and every vertical wall standing on it, `face:0x…` ids from `list_features`, all on one model) and adds it as a document tool. Give `undersize` (mm per side, 0 or more) or `condition` (a machine EDM condition id, read from the setup's sinker EDM; `setup` names that setup, default the active one), not both; `stub` (more than 0) is how far the electrode stands above the cavity's mouth; `pickup` (0 or more) is the offset from the electrode's top to the measuring reference. `orbit` makes it that much smaller again per side. The reply gives the electrode, its `burn` fields (the `add_operation` params of a Sinker Burn of this cavity) a `warning` when the stated undersize is 0 (the electrode is then the cavity's full size, so any spark gap burns the walls past it), and a `note` when an orbit is given. Only an axis-aligned rectangular cavity yields an electrode; refused by name: picks on more than one model or on something that is not a face, a degenerate face, a boss, rib or overhang standing in the electrode's way, a condition with no undersize or no sinker EDM setup, a model whose facets can't be read, and malformed numbers. One undo step.
-- `edit_operation { "name": string, "params": object }`: JSON merge-patch operation parameters (e.g. `stepdown`, `stepover`, `feed`, `spindle_speed`).
+- `edit_operation { "name": string, "params": object }`: JSON merge-patch operation parameters (e.g. `stepdown`, `stepover`, `feed`, `spindle_speed`). Give flat fields: `{"name":"Pocket1","params":{"stepdown":0.75}}`, not the kind wrapper returned by `get_job`. A single matching wrapper such as `{"pocket":{"stepdown":0.75}}` is still refused. If its flat patch passes the edit checks, the refusal ends with `Corrected call: edit_operation ` and JSON arguments that preserve the requested name and patch values. Retry those arguments. Mismatched kinds, extra outer keys, unknown fields and invalid values remain refused without a corrected call. Refusal does not change the parameters or undo history.
 - **Change a lead shape (#2876)**: `add_operation` and `edit_operation` merge object keys, including enum shape keys. Inspect the current shape with `get_job`, or the seeded defaults with `list_operation_types`. To change a linear lead to an arc, give `"params": { "lead": { "linear": null, "arc": { "radius": 3.0 } } }`. Remove the old key with `null` in the same patch. For a nested lead, give `"params": { "links": { "approach": { "lead_out": { "linear": null, "arc": { "radius": 3.0 } } } } }`. Without removal, the refusal keeps the parser error and lists the merged field paths and keys, such as `lead: arc, linear`.
 - **Pass starts at (#3316)**: `edit_operation { "name": "O1", "params": { "pass_start": "outside" } }` sets where each level's rings start on a 2D Offset: `"auto"` (the default, the core first; the reply leaves the key out), `"inside"` (the part or island wall first) or `"outside"` (the outer edge first; with an Outside containment the stock edge, so each level starts in air). Inside and Outside cut rings that follow the start edge one stepover at a time; where the first ring runs along a wall, or the area is narrower than the tool plus one stepover, a cut takes the full tool width and the toolpath carries a `Pass start` note (a warning line on the op page). Any other word is refused. One undo step. The same key is on 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive, Circular, Bore, 3D Pocket and 3D Finish (#3354, #3355, #3359, #3360, #3361, #3362), through the same `edit_operation` door. Absent means `"auto"`. The project file does not write `"auto"`, and the reply leaves it out. Where the choice is not used, the app says so: 2D Pocket with Zigzag rows or with rest machining, and 3D Pocket with the Zigzag or Auto strategy, with rest machining, or with the Adaptive (HSM) strategy, carry a `Pass starts at` note and cut in the Auto order. A 3D Finish reads the key only for the Contour and Flat patterns (the op page says that the other patterns have no ring order). 2D Adaptive with the Trochoidal method refuses `"inside"` and `"outside"` by name, at the edit and again at `generate`; use `"auto"` there. Face, Slot and Trochoidal Slot refuse the key by name (no inside or outside order). Any other kind refuses it as an unknown field.
 - **Approach distance (#3745)**: `edit_operation { "name": "P1", "params": { "links": { "approach": { "approach_distance": 5.0 } } } }` sets how far outside the stock edge, in mm, the entry of an Inside or Outside pass goes down to the cut depth in air. The default is 2.0 mm; the project file and the reply leave the key out at the default. Zero is legal; a negative or non-finite value is refused by name on creation and edit. One undo step. The Lead in / Lead out page shows it as "Approach distance" on 2D Offset, 2D Pocket and 2D Adaptive when Pass starts at is Inside or Outside. The entry that reads it comes with #3746; until then the value is stored and changes no move.
